{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-03T10:25:08.351Z","author":"toolchain-web-1103","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"dea03de07548ea698db91bc1","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-03T10:25:08.351Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-03T10:25:08.351Z","author":"toolchain-web-1103","text":"Root cause 1 (test fixture pinned old CLI behaviour): pm-cli GH-1617 (2026.10.30, Fixed) made history display order explicit. 'pm history <id> --compact' now returns newest-first rows with order:\"newest_first\"; the old versions returned an unlabeled oldest-first stream. The projection test fixture reversed compact_history and relabeled it newest_first, which under the new CLI yields oldest-first rows mislabeled newest_first; normalizeItemHistory correctly returns them newest-first and the deepEqual against the chronological expectation fails. The production reader readItemHistoryPage is unaffected because it consumes --full output (default oldest_first with an explicit label) and the normalizer honors the label. Plan: update the fixture to the new delivery contract and additionally request --order oldest_first explicitly in the page reader so the route contract no longer depends on the per-mode default."}]}],"before_hash":"aa12ab324ea24b1deb55a9b5a033bdfa83a7fa35ae72cd73418fcc2123ab29a2","after_hash":"883f293b74531011bc9fb83e6e6cd1012d5c7b91df858d867ce367818ae408ac","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"b7b40ba466801bdf7430be10988ea1a54eeda507b414b7251d017614df6c8593"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-03T10:29:00.474Z","author":"toolchain-web-1103","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"dea03de07548ea698db91bc1","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-03T10:29:00.473Z","author":"toolchain-web-1103","text":"Fix 1 (production hardening): readRows in src/services/item-history.ts now passes --order oldest_first on every host history read. The route contract (ItemHistoryPage.order = oldest_first) previously relied on the --full projection default; GH-1617 made order an explicit host choice, so pm-web requests its contract instead of inheriting a mode default that upstream could change. Verified through the real SDK dispatcher: the route-level pagination tests (bounded pages, stale cursors, 60 adversarial append schedules) pass on 2026.10.30 with the flag."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-03T10:29:00.474Z"}],"before_hash":"883f293b74531011bc9fb83e6e6cd1012d5c7b91df858d867ce367818ae408ac","after_hash":"cc19871366f0910b2af42c669fad5ce89187143df5b17f2b0bbfdf1fd0bdabaa","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"9ab492cc0c7ef28f595d0422885281a2bd02952eaa1366eb25b45b6ba19dd2ca"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-03T10:29:02.345Z","author":"toolchain-web-1103","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"dea03de07548ea698db91bc1","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-03T10:29:02.345Z","author":"toolchain-web-1103","text":"Fix 2 (test fixture updated to the new contract, intent kept): test/item-history-projection.test.ts asserted the normalizer against a fixture built by reversing compact_history, which assumed the pre-2026.10.30 unlabeled oldest-first compact stream. Under 2026.10.30 the compact projection arrives newest-first with order:newest_first, so the reversed fixture became oldest-first rows mislabeled newest_first and the normalizer correctly returned newest-first. The fixture now asserts the delivered order label (newest_first), checks normalized indices 1..4, and feeds the complementary oldest-first fixture; the timestamp-tie fixture derives from the oldest-first rows so delivered order still survives ties. No assertion was deleted; the refusal, tie and transport-failure coverage is unchanged."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-03T10:29:02.345Z"}],"before_hash":"cc19871366f0910b2af42c669fad5ce89187143df5b17f2b0bbfdf1fd0bdabaa","after_hash":"8c5efd57e78d2f14505e0d8eb21058a663ee03a53b107ffe49adcef56ed570a3","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"ffd18c8e0d399e3b1025548c20f9486fd9921acc6eb876976881f4b5e25b6ca4"}
